146	## Diff Command
147	
148	```
149	diff
150	  Generate a BOM diff
151	
152	Usage:
153	  cyclonedx diff <from-file> <to-file> [options]
154	
155	Arguments:
156	  <from-file>  From BOM filename.
157	  <to-file>    To BOM filename.
158	
159	Options:
160	  --from-format <autodetect|json|protobuf|xml>  Specify from file format.
161	  --to-format <autodetect|json|protobuf|xml>    Specify to file format.
162	  --output-format <json|text>                   Specify output format (defaults to text).
163	  --component-versions                          Report component versions that have been added, removed or modified.
164	  --semantic, --semantic-diff                   Report semantic changes to components, versions and dependency edges.
165	```
166	
167	### Examples
168	
169	Reporting on components with version changes:  
170	`cyclonedx-cli diff sbom-from.xml sbom-to.xml --component-versions`
171	
172	Reporting semantic changes while filtering generator metadata noise:
173	
174	`cyclonedx-cli diff sbom-from.json sbom-to.json --semantic`
175	
176	The semantic diff matches components by PURL (ignoring the version) or by
177	group/name. It reports added and removed components, version changes, and
178	added and removed dependency edges. Dependency edges are also compared by
179	component identity, so a version bump does not make the complete dependency
180	graph appear changed.
181	
182	`metadata.timestamp` and generator tool version changes are classified as
183	noise. They are returned in a separate `noise` collection and are never
184	included in the semantic change counts.
185	
186	The default `diff` output is semantic. The legacy
187	`--component-versions` option keeps its existing text and JSON output, and
188	can be combined with `--semantic` when both reports are required.
